    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="1034" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg924"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11681: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-19T12:00:00+08:00">December 19,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received December 19—5:28 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>My December 19, 9 a.m. I have just had a talk with C. C. Wu who tells me that the
                    Government is going to be very much preoccupied with governmental reorganization
                    during next 2 weeks. He said that posts of Foreign Affairs and Finance in new
                    Cabinet were extremely uncertain. He himself expects to take Chairmanship of
                    Kwangtung.</p>
                <p>I told him, as I told Koo yesterday, that I was going north on Monday<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d833-f1"/> to return shortly after the new year.</p>
                <p>I and my French colleagues are expecting to dine informally with General Chiang
                    Kai-shek Sunday evening. My British colleague leaves Shanghai today by Japanese
                    merchant vessel for Tientsin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
